# `len(x)` at an int, written INSIDE an f-string hole. Until 2026-09-04 tychoc1
# kept the hole as raw text and accepted this; the expect line pins the whole
# message, which both compilers now print at the same line.
# expect: len(...) takes an array, a string, bytes, a map, or a soa
fn main():
    x := 5
    print(f"{len(x)}\n")
